ation is already solved for $a:$\n\n$$\na=7\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=7$ into $3a+6b=15,$ then we can find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+6b & =15 \\\\ 3(7)+6b & =15 \\\\ 6b & =-6 \\\\ b & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=7,\\,b=-1.$ So,\n\n$$\na-b=7-(-1)=7+1=8.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546991 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546991 #edb/ref 1069 "q-18555" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546991 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546991 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a+b?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2b=6a+14 \\\\ 5b+25=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546991 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3b789afd-79c7-56fc-b94a-f894f177dfe2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546991 #edb/ref 1074 "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2b=6a+14 & \\,\\,(1) \\\\ 5b+25=0. & \\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(2),$ we can solve for $b$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5b+25 & =0 \\\\ 5b & =-25 \\\\ b & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-5$ into equation $(1)$ and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-5) & =6a+14 \\\\ -10 & =6a+14 \\\\ -10-14 & =6a \\\\ 6a & =-24 \\\\ a & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-4,\\,b=-5.$ So,\n\n$$\na+b=-4+(-5)=-4-5=-9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547088 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186547152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547088 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0a9225c0-5f39-5569-928a-3834451e9d52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547088 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186074185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547152 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186547164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547152 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ca7de6